data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1454,"item_id":"fc_056abd335d7a6d53016adb405b66748191a1e77b9d54e9952f","output_index":2,"arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"inference\":\"R001\",\"packet_sha256\":\"f42b4fa9d77ce4e6155682ed6b5c70fc192fea79ac287cda504c200f84155926\",\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"Fresh packet-only mathematical review: I read packet.json in full and the declared Audit A, self-containment, and format rules. The mathematical boundary was this packet plus those procedural rules; I did not use a source proof, another inference body, prior audit, or outside mathematical task material. Carrier identity and canonical-hash/transmission binding are outside this review, so I make no runtime attestation. First unsupported implication: S003 uses rank_R(J) and concludes n=n rank_R(J), hence rank one, although the packet defines rank_R only for a finite free R-module and has not proved J finite free; it also supplies no local justification of the rank/tensor additivity step here. The later fractional-ideal argument depends on the asserted rank-one identification, so it cannot repair this order of proof. This blocks acceptance without asserting the target theorem is false.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The cited H001–H004 statements are present in the packet and are the only graph inputs. Their stated prime, characteristic, weight-range, module, and representation conditions supply the hypotheses used in the written argument; no external result is cited.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0\",\"/inputs/1\",\"/inputs/2\",\"/inputs/3\",\"/inference/inputs\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The first unsupported step occurs in S003: from the direct-sum decomposition and tensoring with Q, the text asserts n=n rank_R(J), hence J has rank one. But rank_R was defined only for a finite free R-module, and S003 has not established that J is finite free. The tensor/rank identity is also asserted rather than derived there. The subsequent Q-linear identification and ideal-principality reasoning rely on this rank-one step. Later steps cannot cure this earlier gap.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/22\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"S003 imports an unestablished rank computation/finite-free-module property in the claim n=n rank_R(J), and then invokes a Q-linear identification based on rank one. The calculation-policy text names localization and elementary ideal calculations but cannot import these omitted facts or expand the definition of rank_R.\",\"locations\":[\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inference/locals/22\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"P states the complete desired conclusion: nonzero M tensor_Z K and the invariant-subspace criterion for x,y,h. S008 purports to conclude that statement, with no altered endpoint or quantifier apparent. This statement match does not overcome the failed derivation.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/7/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The nonzero assumption L1 is introduced in S005 and declared discharged in S008. F002 and F003 record L1 as an open assumption; the selected witnesses are used in the nonzero branch. The packet's branch bookkeeping is intelligible, though scope bookkeeping does not prove the mathematical steps.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/29\",\"/inference/argument/4\",\"/inference/argument/5/produces/0\",\"/inference/argument/6/produces/0\",\"/inference/argument/7\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no E/M inputs or applications requiring source-theorem bindings. The direct H inputs are used for the stated representation, parameter, and module facts; the identified rank issue is a local argument gap, not a source-application problem.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/applications\",\"/inference/argument/0\",\"/inference/argument/2\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The H statements and target are stated in full within the packet. The local facts used in later paragraphs are given explicit F statements; the relevant definitions and parameter meanings are present. The identified defect is inferential, not a missing target/input formula.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inputs/2/statement\",\"/inputs/3/statement\",\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"UNVERIFIED\",\"notes\":\"The proof declares many of its local objects and the principal basis, module, and matrix-unit constructions are traceable. However, the rank computation uses rank_R(J) before the packet has established that J meets rank_R's stated finite-free domain. Thus that occurrence is not supported by the declared definition/domain. I do not treat the inventory itself as proof of all prose occurrences.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/22\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/locals/21\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The factual claim n=n rank_R(J), used to conclude rank one, has no established premise within S003 or a direct input. The packet's calculation policy cannot stand in for that missing derivation. Descendant steps relying on this claim are therefore not closed.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\",\"/inference/argument/3/text\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"This replay was conducted using only the supplied frozen packet and the declared Yui procedure; no source proof, other R body, prior audit, or answer key was supplied/read. On that packet alone, S003's rank step and its required finite-free/rank justification are absent, so the argument is insufficient for acceptance. I state no attestation of carrier identity, isolation mechanism, or canonical transmission binding; those are expressly outside this mathematical review.\",\"locations\":[\"/warning\",\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"/inference/locals/22\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/2/text\",\"premises\":\"S003 has M_R=direct_sum_i J e_i; M_R is finite free of rank n; and Q is the fraction field of R.\",\"conclusion\":\"n=n rank_R(J), hence J has rank one, followed by a Q-linear identification Q tensor_R J=Q.\",\"judgment\":\"Unsupported in this packet at this point: rank_R is defined for finite free R-modules, but J has not yet been shown finite free, and no local rank/tensor calculation justifies the displayed equality. The later finite-generation, ideal, and principal-ideal discussion uses the rank-one consequence rather than supplying the missing prior justification.\"}]}}"}

